('127.569.d.6.D',3,'A restaurant where guests serve themselves from a long line of hot dishes offers:','["table service", "room service", "buffet service", "drive-through"]'::jsonb,2,'Buffets let guests choose and serve their own food.','original'),
('127.569.d.6.D',4,'Ordering at a counter and receiving food in a bag at a window describes:','["buffet service", "fine dining", "banquet service", "fast food service"]'::jsonb,3,'Quick-service restaurants emphasize speed and convenience.','original'),
('127.569.d.6.E',3,'In a standard place setting, the forks are placed on the guest''s:','["left", "right", "head", "lap"]'::jsonb,0,'Forks go to the left of the plate; knives and spoons to the right.','original'),
('127.569.d.6.E',4,'A clean, properly arranged place setting shows guests the restaurant''s attention to:','["distance", "detail", "weather", "rumors"]'::jsonb,1,'Careful table settings create a positive first impression.','original'),
('127.569.d.6.F',3,'Servers should carry plates and serve food from a guest''s left, while beverages are served from the:','["floor", "ceiling", "right", "kitchen"]'::jsonb,2,'In American-style service, food is served from the left and drinks from the right.','original'),
('127.569.d.6.F',4,'Clearing plates only after everyone at the table has finished eating is a service technique that shows:','["haste", "doubt", "anger", "courtesy"]'::jsonb,3,'Waiting avoids making slower diners feel rushed.','original'),
('127.569.d.7.A',3,'Under the law, employers must provide a workplace free of recognized:','["hazards", "uniforms", "profits", "menus"]'::jsonb,0,'Employers are responsible for a safe workplace.','original'),
('127.569.d.7.A',4,'Workers help keep a workplace safe by following rules and reporting unsafe:','["menus", "conditions", "holidays", "profits"]'::jsonb,1,'Workers share responsibility by speaking up about dangers.','original'),
('127.569.d.7.B',3,'The federal agency that sets and enforces workplace safety standards is:','["the FDA", "the IRS", "OSHA", "NASA"]'::jsonb,2,'OSHA stands for Occupational Safety and Health Administration.','original'),
('127.569.d.7.B',4,'OSHA standards exist to reduce workplace injuries, illnesses, and:','["wages", "profits", "breaks", "fatalities"]'::jsonb,3,'The goal is to protect workers from serious harm and death.','original'),
('127.569.d.7.C',3,'Industrial hygiene focuses on recognizing and controlling workplace health hazards such as noise, chemicals, and:','["fumes", "tips", "menus", "uniforms"]'::jsonb,0,'Industrial hygienists measure and reduce exposure to harmful agents.','original'),
('127.569.d.7.C',4,'A kitchen exhaust hood that removes smoke and grease vapors is an engineering control that protects workers'' health by improving:','["menu variety", "air quality", "table turnover", "tip income"]'::jsonb,1,'Ventilation removes harmful airborne particles.','original'),
('127.569.d.7.D',3,'Raw chicken juices touching a salad is an example of cross-contamination and a common source of food-borne:','["flavor", "profit", "illness", "menu"]'::jsonb,2,'Cross-contamination spreads pathogens to ready-to-eat foods.','original'),
('127.569.d.7.D',4,'Cooking food to the correct internal temperature and washing hands often help prevent:','["slow service", "tip loss", "staff turnover", "food-borne illness"]'::jsonb,3,'Proper cooking and hygiene stop pathogens from reaching guests.','original'),
('127.569.d.7.E',3,'Cut-resistant gloves worn when using a slicer are an example of personal protective:','["equipment", "etiquette", "policy", "recipe"]'::jsonb,0,'PPE protects workers from specific hazards.','original'),
('127.569.d.7.E',4,'Slip-resistant shoes protect kitchen workers from:','["sunburn", "falls", "boredom", "hunger"]'::jsonb,1,'Kitchen floors get wet and greasy, so traction matters.','original'),
('127.569.d.7.F',3,'Keeping aisles clear of boxes and cords helps prevent trips and:','["holidays", "profits", "falls", "rewards"]'::jsonb,2,'Clear walkways reduce the risk of injury.','original'),
('127.569.d.7.F',4,'Placing a wet-floor sign after mopping warns coworkers of a slippery:','["recipe", "menu", "schedule", "surface"]'::jsonb,3,'Warning signs prevent slips on wet floors.','original'),
('127.569.d.7.G',3,'A frayed power cord on a mixer is an electrical hazard that could cause shock or:','["fire", "praise", "profit", "rain"]'::jsonb,0,'Damaged cords can spark and overheat.','original'),
('127.569.d.7.G',4,'Water and electricity do not mix, so workers should never touch plugged-in equipment with wet:','["plans", "hands", "schedules", "menus"]'::jsonb,1,'Wet hands increase the risk of electric shock.','original'),
('127.569.d.7.H',3,'Cleaning chemicals should be stored away from food and kept in clearly labeled:','["suitcases", "drawers", "containers", "envelopes"]'::jsonb,2,'Labels identify contents and hazards.','original'),
('127.569.d.7.H',4,'Mixing bleach with ammonia can release dangerous:','["colors", "coupons", "flavors", "gases"]'::jsonb,3,'Never mix cleaning chemicals; toxic gases can form.','original'),
('127.569.d.7.I',3,'A Safety Data Sheet explains a chemical''s hazards and how to respond to a:','["spill", "sale", "holiday", "review"]'::jsonb,0,'SDS documents list first aid and cleanup instructions.','original'),
('127.569.d.7.I',4,'Evacuation maps and exit signs help employees leave the building safely during a:','["sale", "crisis", "delivery", "meeting"]'::jsonb,1,'Posted routes make it easier to exit quickly.','original'),
('127.569.d.7.J',3,'A good safety and health program includes management leadership, worker participation, and hazard:','["decoration", "hiding", "identification", "avoidance"]'::jsonb,2,'Finding hazards is the first step in controlling them.','original'),
('127.569.d.7.J',4,'Regular safety meetings let employees share concerns and learn about new:','["uniforms", "desserts", "recipes", "procedures"]'::jsonb,3,'Meetings keep everyone current on safe work practices.','original'),
('127.569.d.7.K',3,'A written document that tells employees how to evacuate and whom to call is an emergency action:','["plan", "menu", "bill", "tip"]'::jsonb,0,'Written plans guide everyone during emergencies.','original'),
('127.569.d.7.K',4,'Keeping grease cleaned from hoods and stoves is a fire prevention step that lowers the risk of:','["low sales", "kitchen fires", "food waste", "slow orders"]'::jsonb,1,'Grease buildup is a common cause of kitchen fires.','original'),
