from (values
('127.569.d.10.E',3,'In a job interview, a good way to answer ''Tell me about yourself'' is to give a brief, focused summary of your skills and:','["experience", "vacation plans", "opinions about coworkers", "complaints"]'::jsonb,0,'Interviewers want to hear relevant qualifications.','original'),
('127.569.d.10.E',4,'After an interview, sending a short thank-you note to the interviewer shows:','["desperation", "professionalism", "rivalry", "laziness"]'::jsonb,1,'A thank-you note leaves a positive impression.','original'),
('127.569.d.10.F',3,'A personal training plan to become a sous chef lists the skills to learn, the classes to take, and the target:','["colors", "songs", "dates", "rumors"]'::jsonb,2,'Target dates keep progress on track.','original'),
('127.569.d.10.F',4,'Setting short-term and long-term goals in a training plan helps a person reach a specific:','["hobby", "holiday", "vacation", "occupation"]'::jsonb,3,'A plan links learning steps to a career goal.','original'),
('127.569.d.10.G',3,'Studying how many restaurant jobs are open and what they pay in your region is called analyzing the local labor:','["market", "map", "menu", "vote"]'::jsonb,0,'The labor market is the supply and demand for workers.','original'),
('127.569.d.10.G',4,'A growing city with many new restaurants likely has strong demand for:','["farm equipment", "restaurant workers", "ship captains", "miners"]'::jsonb,1,'New restaurants need cooks, servers, and managers.','original'),
('127.569.d.10.H',3,'Attending a workshop on new cooking techniques is an example of professional:','["dismissal", "decline", "development", "retirement"]'::jsonb,2,'Professional development builds new skills.','original'),
('127.569.d.10.H',4,'To stay current on industry trends, a manager might subscribe to a trade:','["fine", "penalty", "uniform", "magazine"]'::jsonb,3,'Trade publications report news and trends.','original'),
('127.569.d.10.I',3,'A person who starts and runs a food truck business is an:','["entrepreneur", "customer", "employee", "inspector"]'::jsonb,0,'Entrepreneurs start and operate their own businesses.','original'),
('127.569.d.10.I',4,'An entrepreneur takes on the risk of a new business in hopes of earning a:','["fine", "profit", "penalty", "warning"]'::jsonb,1,'Risk-taking aims at rewards such as profit.','original'),
('127.569.d.11.A',3,'Fast-food chains grew rapidly in the United States after the spread of cars and:','["castles", "canoes", "highways", "telescopes"]'::jsonb,2,'Automobile travel created demand for quick roadside meals.','original'),
('127.569.d.11.A',4,'Early public eating places such as roadside inns mostly served:','["lawyers", "chefs only", "astronauts", "travelers"]'::jsonb,3,'Inns provided food and lodging to people on the road.','original'),
('127.569.d.11.B',3,'Sushi, tacos, and pizza are found in many countries because of globalization and cultural:','["exchange", "laws", "isolation", "taxes"]'::jsonb,0,'Travel and trade spread foods around the world.','original'),
('127.569.d.11.B',4,'Restaurants in a diverse city often offer dishes from many different:','["budgets", "cultures", "planets", "decades"]'::jsonb,1,'Diverse communities bring varied cuisines.','original'),
('127.569.d.11.C',3,'Many restaurants now offer online ordering and delivery apps. This is a growing industry:','["rumor", "error", "trend", "penalty"]'::jsonb,2,'A trend is a general direction in which something is developing.','original'),
('127.569.d.11.C',4,'Using ingredients from nearby farms appeals to guests who want fresher, locally grown:','["tires", "rugs", "paint", "food"]'::jsonb,3,'Farm-to-table sourcing is a current trend.','original'),
('127.569.d.12.A',3,'Ordering too much perishable food can lead to spoilage and lost:','["money", "guests", "chairs", "windows"]'::jsonb,0,'Wasted food is wasted spending.','original'),
('127.569.d.12.A',4,'Counting stock on a regular schedule helps a restaurant avoid running out of items and:','["serving", "overstocking", "smiling", "cleaning"]'::jsonb,1,'Accurate counts balance supply with demand.','original'),
('127.569.d.12.B',3,'Washing pots, pans, and dishes and keeping the kitchen sanitary is the job of a kitchen:','["sommelier", "pastry chef", "steward", "host"]'::jsonb,2,'Stewards keep tools clean and the kitchen sanitary.','original'),
('127.569.d.12.B',4,'Proper stewarding procedures keep kitchen tools sanitized and ready for:','["sale", "display", "rent", "use"]'::jsonb,3,'Clean equipment is ready when cooks need it.','original'),
('127.569.d.12.C',3,'Using first in, first out (FIFO) when storing food reduces waste and helps protect:','["profits", "menus", "dishes", "chairs"]'::jsonb,0,'Rotating stock prevents spoiled inventory.','original'),
('127.569.d.12.C',4,'Storing raw meat below ready-to-eat food in the cooler prevents drips that cause cross-contamination and costly:','["sales", "waste", "praise", "tips"]'::jsonb,1,'Proper storage prevents contamination and loss.','original'),
('127.569.d.12.D',3,'A restaurant adds a markup to the cost of ingredients to cover labor, overhead, and:','["taxes only", "nothing", "profit", "rent only"]'::jsonb,2,'Menu prices must cover all costs plus a profit.','original'),
('127.569.d.12.D',4,'Food cost percentage is found by dividing food cost by:','["labor hours", "table count", "menu pages", "food sales"]'::jsonb,3,'Food cost % = food cost / food sales.','original'),
('127.569.d.12.E',3,'Guests who return often and recommend a restaurant to friends show customer:','["loyalty", "doubt", "anger", "debt"]'::jsonb,0,'Loyal customers support steady sales.','original'),
('127.569.d.12.E',4,'A loyalty program that rewards repeat visits helps a restaurant keep customers and increase:','["turnover", "revenue", "waste", "complaints"]'::jsonb,1,'Repeat customers generate income.','original'),
('127.571.d.1.A',3,'A planner''s firm handshake and welcoming smile when meeting a client are examples of:','["budget reports", "written contracts", "nonverbal communication", "email marketing"]'::jsonb,2,'Gestures and expressions communicate without words.','original'),
('127.571.d.1.A',4,'A planner clearly explaining the event schedule to the catering team is using effective:','["gossip", "guesswork", "silent treatment", "verbal communication"]'::jsonb,3,'Spoken instructions must be clear so everyone knows the plan.','original'),
('127.571.d.1.B',3,'A one-page executive summary sent to a client is a formal way to summarize event:','["details", "gossip", "rumors", "jokes"]'::jsonb,0,'Formal summaries are written and organized.','original'),
('127.571.d.1.B',4,'Giving a coworker a quick verbal recap of a client call in the hallway is an informal:','["invoice", "summary", "contract", "audit"]'::jsonb,1,'Informal summaries are brief and spoken.','original'),
('127.571.d.1.C',3,'A planner combines notes from the client, the venue, and the caterer into one plan. This is called:','["canceling an event", "ignoring details", "synthesizing information", "copying a menu"]'::jsonb,2,'Synthesizing means merging information from several sources.','original'),
('127.571.d.1.C',4,'When several tasks are due, a planner decides which are most important and handles those:','["twice", "last", "never", "first"]'::jsonb,3,'Prioritizing puts the most important tasks at the front.','original'),
('127.571.d.1.D',3,'A client says the event should be ''casual.'' The planner asks, ''What does casual look like to you?'' This is using active listening to:','["clarify", "dismiss", "interrupt", "argue"]'::jsonb,0,'Clarifying questions prevent misunderstandings.','original'),
('127.571.d.1.D',4,'Taking notes while a client speaks helps a planner obtain accurate:','["discounts", "information", "tickets", "souvenirs"]'::jsonb,1,'Notes capture details the planner will need later.','original'),
('127.571.d.1.E',3,'A presentation meant to convince a client to book your venue is a:','["instructional presentation", "informative presentation", "persuasive presentation", "entertaining presentation"]'::jsonb,2,'Persuasive presentations aim to influence a decision.','original'),
('127.571.d.1.E',4,'A presentation that teaches new staff how to set up a banquet room is:','["decorative", "persuasive", "fictional", "instructional"]'::jsonb,3,'Instructional presentations teach how to do a task.','original'),
('127.571.d.1.F',3,'Planners work with internal customers, such as coworkers, and external customers, such as:','["clients", "regulators", "landlords", "competitors"]'::jsonb,0,'External customers are the people or groups who hire the planner.','original'),
('127.571.d.1.F',4,'Being courteous and dependable with both coworkers and clients helps maintain strong:','["deadlines", "relationships", "invoices", "deposits"]'::jsonb,1,'Positive interactions build trust.','original'),
('127.571.d.1.G',3,'A signed agreement listing services, dates, and costs for an event is a:','["itinerary", "menu", "contract", "floor plan"]'::jsonb,2,'A contract sets out what each party will provide and pay.','original'),
('127.571.d.1.G',4,'The ''BEO'' used by banquet teams stands for Banquet Event:','["Orchestra", "Outlook", "Office", "Order"]'::jsonb,3,'A BEO details the requirements for an event.','original'),
('127.571.d.2.A',3,'A venue charges $25 per guest for a buffet. What is the cost for 80 guests?','["$2,000", "$3,200", "$200", "$1,000"]'::jsonb,0,'25 x 80 = 2,000.','original'),
('127.571.d.2.A',4,'A $4,000 event has a 7% service charge. How much is the charge?','["$28", "$280", "$70", "$2,800"]'::jsonb,1,'0.07 x 4,000 = 280.','original'),
('127.571.d.2.B',3,'Dividing an event''s total expenses by the number of people who came gives the cost per:','["hour", "sponsor", "person", "room"]'::jsonb,2,'Cost per person is a common event ratio.','original'),
('127.571.d.2.B',4,'A budget compares planned income with planned:','["speeches", "guests", "rooms", "expenses"]'::jsonb,3,'Budgets show whether spending fits expected revenue.','original'),
('127.571.d.2.C',3,'Reading a hotel contract carefully before signing it uses advanced reading skills to avoid unexpected:','["fees", "guests", "songs", "views"]'::jsonb,0,'Careful reading catches hidden charges and rules.','original'),
('127.571.d.2.C',4,'Writing a clear proposal for a client uses strong writing skills to explain the event''s:','["weather", "services", "history", "traffic"]'::jsonb,1,'Proposals describe what the planner will provide.','original'),
('127.571.d.2.D',3,'A chart shows registrations rising each week before a conference. A planner can use this trend to estimate final:','["rent", "weather", "attendance", "tips"]'::jsonb,2,'Trends help predict how many will attend.','original'),
('127.571.d.2.D',4,'A bar graph of past event costs can help a planner find which expense category is the:','["quietest", "coldest", "oldest", "largest"]'::jsonb,3,'The tallest bar shows the biggest cost.','original'),
('127.571.d.2.E',3,'Planners often add a contingency of 5 to 10 percent to a budget to cover unexpected:','["costs", "guests", "themes", "speakers"]'::jsonb,0,'A contingency fund protects against surprise expenses.','original'),
('127.571.d.2.E',4,'Forecasting attendance using past events helps a planner order the right amount of food and:','["songs", "supplies", "weather", "clouds"]'::jsonb,1,'Better forecasts reduce waste and shortages.','original'),
('127.571.d.3.A',3,'Meeting Professionals International (MPI) is an example of a professional:','["venue", "caterer", "association", "penalty"]'::jsonb,2,'Associations support people in a field.','original'),
('127.571.d.3.A',4,'Joining an association gives planners access to training, networking, and industry:','["penalties", "debts", "rumors", "resources"]'::jsonb,3,'Members get tools, education, and contacts.','original'),
('127.571.d.3.B',3,'A planner who sets a goal to earn a new certification this year is creating a personal:','["training plan", "menu", "guest list", "seating chart"]'::jsonb,0,'A training plan outlines steps for professional growth.','original'),
('127.571.d.3.B',4,'To keep current on trends, a planner''s training plan might include reading industry publications and attending:','["races", "conferences", "auctions", "parades"]'::jsonb,1,'Conferences teach new skills and trends.','original'),
('127.571.d.3.C',3,'A person who plans conferences for a company, a hotel, or a nonprofit might work as a meeting or event:','["pilot", "pharmacist", "planner", "welder"]'::jsonb,2,'Planners organize meetings and events.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
