('127.571.d.13.G',4,'Wide aisles and clearly marked exits help move large crowds safely, which is the purpose of effective traffic:','["tickets", "patterns", "jams", "penalties"]'::jsonb,1,'Planned traffic patterns prevent crowding.','original'),
('127.571.d.13.H',3,'Turning over a dining table for the next group of diners at a busy venue is called a table:','["tour", "tax", "rotation", "trade"]'::jsonb,2,'Rotation means resetting and reusing tables.','original'),
('127.571.d.13.H',4,'Efficient table rotation helps a venue serve more guests and increase:','["waste", "errors", "complaints", "revenue"]'::jsonb,3,'More turnover brings more income.','original'),
('127.571.d.13.I',3,'A staffing guide for a banquet shows how many servers, bartenders, and setup crew are needed per:','["guest count", "menu font", "weather report", "color theme"]'::jsonb,0,'Staffing levels depend on how many people attend.','original'),
('127.571.d.13.I',4,'Too few staff at a large event can lead to slow service, while too many can raise labor:','["speakers", "costs", "guests", "menus"]'::jsonb,1,'Staffing must balance service and expense.','original'),
('127.571.d.14.A',3,'Hotels, convention centers, and associations are entities that host or organize meetings and:','["lawsuits", "patrols", "events", "exams"]'::jsonb,2,'Many organizations are part of the industry.','original'),
('127.571.d.14.A',4,'A destination marketing organization promotes a city to attract meetings, conventions, and:','["landfills", "lawsuits", "factories", "tourists"]'::jsonb,3,'These organizations help bring visitors to an area.','original'),
('127.571.d.14.B',3,'A company that pays money to support an event in exchange for advertising is a:','["sponsor", "chaperone", "producer", "guest"]'::jsonb,0,'Sponsors fund events and get exposure.','original'),
('127.571.d.14.B',4,'The group that creates the idea and goals for an event, such as an association hosting its annual conference, is the:','["valet", "organizer", "caterer", "sponsor"]'::jsonb,1,'Organizers decide why and for whom the event is held.','original'),
('127.571.d.14.C',3,'A planner asks three hotels for quotes and pushes for a lower room rate and free meeting space. This is called:','["guessing", "avoiding", "negotiating", "complaining"]'::jsonb,2,'Negotiating means working out better terms.','original'),
('127.571.d.14.C',4,'In negotiations, a planner can often get a better deal by being flexible with dates and booking more:','["tickets", "rumors", "parties", "rooms"]'::jsonb,3,'Volume and flexibility give leverage.','original'),
('127.571.d.14.D',3,'A planner compares the price of a hotel ballroom with a convention center rental and a restaurant''s private room. This is comparing similar:','["services", "rumors", "holidays", "uniforms"]'::jsonb,0,'Comparison shopping helps find the best value.','original'),
('127.571.d.14.D',4,'Audiovisual companies, florists, and caterers are related industries that supply products and services for:','["patrols", "events", "lawsuits", "exams"]'::jsonb,1,'Event planners rely on related industries.','original'),
('127.571.d.14.E',3,'Planning an event at a hotel often includes on-site catering, while planning at a park may require bringing in outside:','["oceans", "mountains", "vendors", "clouds"]'::jsonb,2,'Venues differ in the services they provide.','original'),
('127.571.d.14.E',4,'Compared with a hotel ballroom, a historic museum may have strict rules about food, decorations, and the number of:','["floors", "doors", "clocks", "guests"]'::jsonb,3,'Special venues have unique restrictions.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
